    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill**. **Gunnar Henderson** projects as our premier start with an 81.87 score; despite a neutral park, his combination of an elite batting order spot and a favorable matchup against Spencer Arrighetti allows him to maximize his counting stat potential. **Jackson Merrill** follows closely at 75.26, benefiting from a soft matchup against Dobnak and an aggressive dynamic platoon edge, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** remains a high-floor anchor at 73.66, leveraging a significant 11% boost from J.T. Ginn\u2019s underlying peripherals. We are also monitoring **Miguel Vargas** closely, whose 63.05 score is bolstered by an elite 0.401 xwOBA, positioning him to capitalize against Bieber despite the park factors.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Nasim Nunez**, whose 58.79 score fell just short of displacing our utility options. While **Nasim Nunez** carries the speed profile we crave for this 5x5 build, the optimizer penalized his projected #9 spot in the batting order, which significantly capped his run-scoring probability compared to the stability offered by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** or **Drake Baldwin**. We are maintaining a cautious approach regarding **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker**; both face Ryan Weathers, whose 3.41 xERA represents the toughest test on our board today. The team remains on high alert for lineup confirmation, as several of our starters\u2014specifically **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Curtis Mead**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jackson Merrill**\u2014are currently subject to assumed batting orders that could shift our efficiency calculations if managers deviate from our expectations.",
